      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Partners Gill & Glynn are delighted to bring to the market this well-presented, owner-occupied home, situated just c. 550 metres from Lough Corrib and 5.5 kms from Headford Town. It is also just a short commute (27 kms) north of Galway City. \n\nConstructed in 1998, the property extends to approximately 137 sq.m, and offers well-proportioned accommodation over two floors. To the rear of the main dwelling there is a large outbuilding (71 sq.m.) which would make an ideal studio, home office / gym etc. (See floor plan provided). \n\nThe main dwelling comprises an entrance hall, kitchen/dining room (boasting a Stanley oil range with twin burner), conservatory, living room, ensuite bedroom and shower room. The separate living room is bright and comfortable and features a solid fuel stove. \n\nUpstairs, there are two further spacious bedrooms, both of which benefit from ensuite showrooms. \n\nHeating is by means of oil-fired radiator central heating, stanley oil range and a solid fuel stove. Throughout the house there are attractive features including multiple living areas, a downstairs master bedroom and good levels of natural light.\n\nExternally, the property is approached via an attractive driveway providing generous parking. The rear garden boasts a south/east orientation. The surrounding grounds are laid mainly in lawn and enclosed by mature hedging, providing a good level of privacy and an attractive setting around the residence. The site extends to c. 0.56 acres. \n\nA significant feature of this property is the detached outbuilding extending to approximately 71 sq.m. The building is arranged over two floors and provides substantial additional space. It is connected to water and electricity and offers considerable versatility for a range of uses (subject to the necessary planning).\n\nKeekill is located within easy reach of both Headford and Galway City, providing convenient access to the town and its range of shops, schools, services and amenities. \n\nThis is a well-proportioned property offering comfortable family accommodation together with substantial additional space, making it an appealing option for purchasers seeking a home in a private location close to the shores of Lough Corrib. \n\n\nVIEWING\n\nContact: Claire Glynn at Property Partners Gill & Glynn today by phone, email or WhatsApp on; P: 091 884000 / 087 9655584\n\n\nAttention is drawn to this important notice. \n\n\nProperty Partners Gill & Glynn for themselves and for the vendors or lessors of this property whose agents they are, give notice that:\n\n(i) The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not constitute, nor constitute part of, an offer or contract. \n(ii) All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers or tenants should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. \n(iii) We have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. \n(iv) All measurements are approximate and photographs and maps provided are for guidance only.\n\n\n"
      },
